# Base URL for the API. Usually leave this BLANK.
#
# The app is deployed single-origin: the Express API serves the built SPA, so
# the client talks to the API with relative /api requests (same origin). That
# keeps the auth cookie first-party, which is required for Safari/iOS.
#
# - Local dev: leave blank — the Vite proxy forwards /api -> http://localhost:5000.
# - Production (single Web Service): leave blank — /api is same-origin.
# - Only set this if you intentionally host the client separately from the API
#   (not recommended; reintroduces the third-party-cookie problem).
VITE_API_URL=
